Consider a lawful valk with an ultimate weapon kit:

blessed +6 Greyswandir (melee)
blessed rustproof +6 Excalibur (exploration)
blessed rustproof +6 Mjolnir (missile)
blessed +6 silver saber (secondary)
50 blessed fireproof +6 elven daggers (missile)
(10 quivered, 10 bagged, 30 stashed)
blessed +6 unicorn horn
blessed fireproof +6 pickaxe (autodig)

All 50-50 +5 or +6 depending on the last scroll.

I count 2 to get to foopoof +0, (7*4)-1=27 uncursed
to get to +4, 7 blessed to get to either +5 or
+6.  Total of 36 ?oEW across the entire game.

Fewer if they are all ? were blessed, more if
you ever enchant anything else, fewer if you
never enchant the weapon-tools.  You may want to
enchant Sting, Frost Brand and whatever.  I often
end up the game with enough highly enchanted
spare weapons to have consumed twice that number.
For that matter I could easily end up with a
blessed rustroof +5 spetum for any character who
can get to Skilled in polearms now that I have
learned who polearms work (see a thread around a
month ago "Fun with polearms").

Because the variety of weapons in an ultimate
kit is smaller than the variety of armor in an
ultimate kit (even with an entire spare set of
both), ?oEW are a less limited resource than
?oEA in the long run.  Also, because AC matters
so much in the early game there tends to be a
lot of early inefficient use of ?oEA further
skewing the value of the two types of scrolls.



